            <ArticleTitle>Sacral haemangioma as a cause of coccydynia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>524-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 55-year-old woman with coccydynia due to a sacral mass. The histological diagnosis was haemangioma. The MRI findings and the unusual location of this lesion are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
